WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.179
The day after go-live, the help
desk resets hundreds of passwords,

2
00:00:04.179 --> 00:00:07.763
onboards a dozen people and
changes group memberships.

3
00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:10.263
Every one of those
changes touches a control.

4
00:00:10.263 --> 00:00:14.237
Done through a governed path, the
authorization package stays true.

5
00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:17.501
Done as portal clicks, it
ages with every click.

6
00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:21.004
The case for automation is
volume: at day-two scale,

7
00:00:21.004 --> 00:00:25.362
records assembled by hand are
reconstructions, not evidence.

8
00:00:25.362 --> 00:00:29.282
A control that's designed and
deployed but not operated,

9
00:00:29.282 --> 00:00:33.201
with an owner, a gate, a clock
and an evidence feed, is a hope.

10
00:00:33.201 --> 00:00:37.538
The decision for the CIO and
sponsor: fund that operating layer,

11
00:00:37.538 --> 00:00:40.375
and it's mostly automation, not headcount.

12
00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:41.620
Next, what to buy.
